Looking at the comment, I need to express: if the range is valid (fromIndex ≥ 0, toIndex ≥ 0, fromIndex ≤ toIndex), then every bit at an index outside `[fromIndex, toIndex)` keeps its old value.

The relevant observer here is `get(int bitIndex)`. Bits "outside the range" are those at index `i < fromIndex` or `i >= toIndex` (and `i >= 0` since `get` requires nonnegative indices).

<code>assert (fromIndex >= 0 && toIndex >= 0 && fromIndex <= toIndex) => (\forall int i; i >= 0 && (i < fromIndex || i >= toIndex); this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i)));</code>
